Merzal Tamil Tokenizer (v1.0.0, 64K vocabulary)
Copyright 2026 Merzal

This package contains a trained SentencePiece-style Unigram tokenizer model
(`tokenizer.json`) for Tamil, Tanglish and English. It contains no source text
or corpus data: only the learned vocabulary and merge/score tables are shipped.
The tokenizer software is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).

TRAINING DATA ATTRIBUTION

The tokenizer was trained on token statistics from the following datasets. No
documents from them are redistributed in this package.

| Dataset | Provider | License | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| ai4bharat/sangraha (verified/tam) | AI4Bharat, IIT Madras | CC BY 4.0 | Tamil pretraining text |
| ai4bharat/IndicCorpV2 (ta) | AI4Bharat, IIT Madras | CC0 1.0 | Tamil pretraining text |
| wikimedia/wikipedia (20231101.ta) | Wikimedia Foundation | CC BY-SA 3.0 | Tamil pretraining text |
| HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu (sample-10BT) | Hugging Face | ODC-By 1.0 | English pretraining text |
| google/dakshina (ta, romanized) | Google Research | CC BY-SA 4.0 | Tanglish (romanized Tamil) |
| codeparrot/github-code-clean | Hugging Face | Apache 2.0 | Light code coverage (~5%) |

Attribution: Tamil Wikipedia content is by Wikipedia contributors and is used
under CC BY-SA 3.0. Dakshina is by Google Research (Roark et al., LREC 2020)
and is used under CC BY-SA 4.0. Sangraha and IndicCorpV2 are by AI4Bharat.
FineWeb-Edu is by Hugging Face. GitHub Code Clean is by Hugging Face, derived
from public GitHub repositories.

EVALUATION DATA (NOT TRAINED ON)

Held-out validation used HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2, config `tam_Taml`, split
`test` (Hugging Face, ODC-By 1.0). This corpus is disjoint from every training
source above and was never seen during tokenizer training.

